    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d606">

                <pb facs="0760" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1167</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic">February 1,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 9.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 775</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the Legation’s
                    telegram No. 66, of January 29th, 11 a.m.<anchor n="69" xml:id="d606-f1"/> and
                    to forward copies of the notes exchanged between the Chinese and Japanese
                    authorities relative to the cancellation of the Sino-Japanese Military pact. The
                    Legation has been informed by a reliable source that these texts are
                    correct.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(For the Minister)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. B.
                            Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d606-a1.xml" xpointer="d606-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
